From f2b1716d305e225bc4002f2317c0fb56cdb72b9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: randomkid2 <jayden.mattsson101@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:51:40 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Store MPQ entry names with backslashes

MPQ resolves a file by hashing its name, so a stored name must be byte-for-byte
what the client requests: World\Maps\Expansion01\Expansion01_29_32.adt.
Listfile::FileKey normalises to forward slashes for Noggit's own lookups, and
that normalised form went straight into SFileAddFileEx, so every file written
was filed under a name nothing would ever ask for.

The result was a patch archive with a valid header, correct payload and the
right filename that the client silently ignored -- and MPQ viewers still listed
its contents, because they read the (listfile) rather than hashing, which is
what made it invisible.

Confirmed working in game against a 3.3.5a client.
---
 src/ClientData.cpp |  12 +-
 src/MPQArchive.cpp | 647 +++++++++++++++++++++++----------------------
 2 files changed, 341 insertions(+), 318 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ClientData.cpp b/src/ClientData.cpp
index eb7e1e0..c713f79 100644
--- a/src/ClientData.cpp
+++ b/src/ClientData.cpp
@@ -486,7 +486,17 @@ std::array<int, 2> BlizzardArchive::ClientData::saveLocalFilesToArchive(Archive:
                 if (!full_write_file)
                 {
                     // get internal Wow path
-                    auto wow_path = fs::relative(entry.path(), fs::path(_local_path)).generic_string();
+                    //
+                    // BACKSLASHES, not generic_string(). MPQ looks a file up by HASHING ITS NAME,
+                    // so the stored name has to be byte-for-byte what the client will ask for --
+                    // and the client asks for World\Maps\Expansion01\Expansion01_29_32.adt.
+                    // generic_string() returns forward slashes by definition, which hash to
+                    // something else entirely, so every file written here was filed under a name
+                    // nothing would ever request. The archive listed correctly in any MPQ viewer
+                    // (those read the listfile rather than hashing) and the client silently found
+                    // nothing: valid header, correct payload, right archive name, no effect.
+                    auto wow_path = fs::relative(entry.path(), fs::path(_local_path)).string();
+                    std::replace(wow_path.begin(), wow_path.end(), '/', '\\');
 
                     try
                     {
